:: StoryTitle
The Ninefold Cell

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.5.0",
  "start": "prologue"
}

:: Inklink [config]
kind: game
tags: fantasy ~ puzzle ~ escape room ~ text rpg ~ two heroes
ages: 10..
mode: solo
pov: roland, eldric ~ switch freely
~ order each other within earshot
clock: 0.. ~ shown as "turn"
~ turn ends when pov.all.spent or pov.all.passed
start: oubliette for roland, chapel for eldric
default moves: walk
default clash: none

stat wits: 1..=5
stat might: 1..=5
relation trust: roland, eldric ~ 0..=3 ~ shown as "trust"
fact cleverness: 0 ~ shown as "cleverness"
fact brute_force: 0 ~ shown as "brute force"

map prison: 3 by 3 ~ shows visited
~ orrery      | gallery | gate
~ scriptorium | well    | armory
~ oubliette   | ossuary | chapel
place orrery: "the Orrery"
place gallery: "the Gallery of Guests"
place gate: "the Gate"
place scriptorium: "the Scriptorium"
place well: "the Well of the Eye"
place armory: "the Broken Armory"
place oubliette: "the oubliette"
place ossuary: "the Ossuary"
place chapel: "the defiled chapel"
place threshold: "the threshold" ~ checkpoint
place sanctum: "the Host’s sanctum"

fact grate_up: no
fact unbolted: no
fact portcullis_up: no
fact orrery_unlocked: no
fact chute_found: no
fact rope_down: no

way grate: ossuary - oubliette ~ one way ~ down ~ open when grate_up ~ shown as "the grate"
way bolted_door: ossuary - chapel ~ open when unbolted
way portcullis: ossuary - well ~ open when portcullis_up
way glyph_door: chapel - armory
way study_door: scriptorium - well
way ledge: well - armory ~ one way ~ down ~ shown as "the ledge"
way chute: scriptorium - oubliette ~ one way ~ down ~ hidden until chute_found
way stair: well - gallery
way orrery_door: scriptorium - orrery ~ open when orrery_unlocked
way west_arch: orrery - gallery ~ wide
way east_arch: gallery - gate ~ wide
way spiral: armory - gate
way great_door: gate - threshold
~ open when gate.sun_seal and gate.mouth_seal and gate.scale_seal
way sanctum_stair: threshold - sanctum ~ one way

resource vults: 60 ~ per character ~ refill each chronon
resource hp: per character ~ refill on checkpoint ~ shown as "wounds left"
resource inquests: 3 ~ shared
resource rewinds: 1 ~ per character ~ max 1

rewind: undo
~ moves both
~ to any visited turn or checkpoint
~ keeps knows, trust
~ unseen by hask
checkpoint cells: ~ on death in prison
~ resets world, held, trust, hp
~ keeps knows
~ to oubliette for roland, chapel for eldric
checkpoint threshold: ~ on death in sanctum
~ resets sanctum, hp
~ keeps knows, held, trust
~ to threshold

on death
~ then play again

on cross glyph_door when not (glyph.broken or glyph.frozen)
~ then wound actor 1
~ then play chapel:glyph_fires
~ loud

expect always: not (lumen.taken and lumen.lost)
~ else "Lumen is both drawn and wrecked"

act walk: cost 10 ~ steps 1
act examine: cost 10
act take: cost 10
act read: cost 20 ~ check wits >= 3
act lift: cost 30 ~ check might >= 4
act push: cost 40 ~ check might >= 5
act force: cost 30 ~ check might >= 4 ~ loud
act pick: cost 20 ~ check wits >= 3 ~ quiet ~ requires lockpick
act crank: cost 10
act climb: cost 20
act observe: cost rest ~ min 10 ~ watches here
act strike: cost 20
act guard: cost 20
act together: cost 30 from each ~ requires pov.all here

archetype sword: ~ weapon
archetype lever: ~ fixed
~ fact rusty: no
~ fact oiled: no
~ fact snapped: no
~ fact mended: no
archetype mirror: ~ fixed
~ fact open: yes
~ watches here when self.open

item chain: "fifteen feet of broken manacle chain" ~ rope ~ anchor
item bone_pick: "a finger bone, filed to a point" ~ lockpick
item lamp_oil: "a brass lamp, half full of oil" ~ in scriptorium
item rustblade: "a notched arming sword" ~ like sword ~ in armory ~ hidden until armory.searched
item abelard_sword: "Abelard’s longsword" ~ like sword ~ parries flame ~ in well
item lumen: "Lumen, the holy sword of the Dawn" ~ like sword ~ holy ~ absorbs spells ~ in orrery ~ fixed until orrery.aligned
item heart: "a brass sun that beats" ~ phylactery ~ in orrery ~ fixed until lumen.taken
fact charged: no ~ belongs to lumen
fact cracked: no ~ belongs to heart

clue abelard_name: "Someone named Abelard died in the pit. He scratched a line of the Host’s rhyme into the wall."
clue abelard_vow: "Abelard of the Dawn swore the lich would never have his own blade. “He gave it to the deep.”"
clue far_bolt: "The far door of the Ossuary is bolted on the Ossuary side."
clue glyph_lore: "A glyph is only a ring. Break the ring and it’s just paint." ~ shared by both
clue carpet_sags: "The Scriptorium carpet sags in the middle."
clue statue_rule: "The statues move only when nothing is looking at them." ~ insight
clue lumen_lore: "The rod through the orrery’s sun has a Dawn hilt. It is Lumen, which drinks any spell that strikes it."
clue drinks_magic: "Cantrips die as they near the rod in the orrery."
clue heart_is_life: "The orrery’s sun is warm, and it beats. The Host keeps a mirror on it day and night." ~ insight
clue gave_up: "First the breath went, then the warmth, and last, sleep."
clue rhyme_flame: "Flame for the fool,"
clue rhyme_frost: "and frost for the brave,"
clue rhyme_blink: "a blink for the bold,"
clue rhyme_sun: "and the sun for the grave."
clue lodestone: "A spell of weight, carved under the lectern."

fuse flood: 2 ~ shown as "the water" ~ unlit
~ then kill each in oubliette when not grate.open
fuse collapse: 8 ~ shown as "the ceiling" ~ unlit
~ then kill pov.all when pov.any.in(prison)

character roland: "Roland Vey, scholar and thief" ~ playable ~ wits 4 ~ might 1 ~ hp 1
character eldric: "Ser Eldric of the Long Watch" ~ playable ~ wits 2 ~ might 5 ~ hp 2

npc hask: "the Hollow Host" ~ villain ~ moves none ~ in sanctum
npc knight: "the Knight" ~ like statue ~ weight heavy ~ in gallery
npc widow: "the Widow" ~ like statue ~ weight middling ~ in gallery
npc jester: "the Jester" ~ like statue ~ weight light ~ moves 2 per chronon ~ in orrery

objective escape: "Get out of the Ninefold Cell" ~ done when pov.all.in(threshold)
objective host: "Put the Hollow Host down" ~ after escape ~ done when hask.wards == 0

:: roland [character]
fact rewound: no
--
act spark: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ "a snap of heat and light at a point you can see"
act chill: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ "frost on a surface, or a mouthful of water turned to ice"
act gust: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ "one breath of wind, enough to snuff a candle across a room"
act mend: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ "knits a small break: a torn page, a cracked pin, a split lip"
act tug: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ "an unseen pull on something lighter than a book, within sight"
act hush: cost 10 ~ cantrip ~ quiet ~ "swallows one sound for a moment"

combo ember_lance: spark, gust, spark ~ spell ~ "flame, fanned, then lit into a lance"
~ thaws ice ~ cracks glass
combo rime_shield: chill, mend, chill ~ spell ~ "a shell of ice that heals its own cracks"
~ shields target from the next spell
combo frostglass: chill, gust ~ spell ~ "rimes a mirror over until it shows nothing"
combo thunderclap: hush, gust, spark ~ spell ~ "a swallowed sound, carried, then let go at once"
~ interrupts flame, frost
combo backward_knot: mend, hush, tug, mend ~ spell ~ "ties the hour back on itself"
~ rewind ~ once per day ~ needs two to hold it

act lodestone: cost 30 ~ spell ~ learned from clue lodestone
~ "makes one thing very, very heavy, for one breath"

:: eldric [character]
fact chained: yes
fact blessed: no
fact frozen: no
--
act second_dawn: cost rest ~ min 20 ~ prayer ~ rewind ~ once
~ "Lord of the first light, give us the hour back."
act vigil: cost rest ~ min 20 ~ prayer
hp 3 when self.blessed and here.in(sanctum)

:: hask [npc]
fact deaths: 0 ~ survives death
fact saw_heart: no
fact shown_heart: no
fact grounded: no
fact dodging: no
fact mortal: no
let holder: one(character, holding: heart)
--
starts: sanctum

on start
~ then say self "Nine rooms, two guests, one door. I made every lock myself."

on enter gallery when gallery_mirror.open
~ then say self "(humming) …and frost for the brave…"

on raise cleverness
~ then say self "Oh, nicely done. Nicely."

on raise brute_force
~ then say self "Must you break everything?"

on raise trust
~ then say self "How touching. The thief and the paladin."

on loud when not hushed
~ then say self "Shh. Some of us are working."

on act gallery:mirror
~ then say self "I do like to keep an eye on my children."

on take heart when orrery_mirror.open
~ then say self "PUT. THAT. DOWN."

on death
~ then raise self.deaths 1
~ then say self "Again! From the top!"

on death when self.deaths >= 3
~ then say self "I’m getting bored. Have you tried oil? Oil is very good for rust."
~ once

on death when self.deaths >= 5
~ then say self "The rhyme, you dolts. I hum it for a reason."
~ once

on turn when pov.all.in(oubliette) and not rope_down and not flood.lit
~ then say self "Both of you? In the pit? Oh, this is embarrassing. Here."
~ then set grate_up: yes
~ then set rope_down: yes

on turn when collapse.lit
~ then say self "My house! My lovely house!"

:: statue [archetype]
--
moves: 1 per chronon

goal stalk:
~ toward nearest(living)
~ via wide
~ weight 1
~ when not self.watched

reaction strike:
~ when not self.watched and count(living, in: here) >= 1
~ then kill one(living, in: here)

on enter gate by statue when actor.weight == heavy
~ then set gate.scale_seal: yes
~ then fix actor
~ once

:: prologue [prologue]
The cart stopped at the bottom of the world, and a voice like a delighted host said, “Ah. Guests.”

[after 2s]
They took Roland Vey’s picks, his knives and his good boots. They took Ser Eldric’s sword, his mail and the sun from his surcoat. They did not take the argument the two of them had been having since the road, which Roland was winning.

[after 2s]
“Nine rooms,” said the Hollow Host, from every mirror at once. “One door. I made every lock myself, and I do so love to watch. Die as often as you like. I’ll put you back.”

[note]
Solo play: you are both of them. Switch between them at any moment, for free. Each has sixty vults a turn. Telling the other what to do costs them, not you.

[end]
> [[Wake as Roland, in the pit->oubliette]] ~ become roland
> [[Wake as Eldric, in chains->chapel]] ~ become eldric

:: oubliette [room card:SW]
item abelard: "a knight’s skeleton in a rotted surcoat" ~ fixed ~ holds bone_pick
inquest: "The grate is too heavy for anything you can do from down here." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "Look past the grate. On the far door above, something only needs to slide." ~ wits 3..
--
[if me.is(roland) and me.visits == 1]
You wake on your back at the bottom of a stone throat twelve feet deep. The sky is an iron grate.

[else]
The oubliette: twelve feet of wet stone, and a grate for a lid.

[end]
A pipe in the wall drips into a drain. In the corner sits a skeleton in a rotted surcoat, head tilted, as if waiting for someone to finish a story.

[if rope_down]
Eldric’s chain hangs from the grate, swaying.

[if flood.lit]
Water is roaring out of the pipe. It’s already past your knees.

[end]
> [[Examine the skeleton->oubliette:bones]] ~ examine
> [[Read the scratches by the skeleton->oubliette:scratches]] ~ examine
> [[Look up through the grate->oubliette:look_up]] ~ examine
> [[Tug the bolt across the room->oubliette:tug_bolt]]
~ tug
~ for roland
~ when me.knows.far_bolt and not bolted_door.open
> [[Tug the peg out from under the sluice lever->ossuary:sluice]]
~ tug
~ for roland
~ when me.knows.far_bolt and not well.drained
> [[Climb the chain->oubliette:climb]] ~ climb ~ when rope_down
> [[Throw the chain up and hook the grate->oubliette:hook]] ~ cost 20 ~ when me.holds.chain and grate.open and not rope_down
> [[Boost Roland up to the grate->oubliette:boost]] ~ lift ~ for eldric ~ when roland.here and grate.open and not rope_down

:: oubliette:bones [act]
learn abelard_name
gain bone_pick when me.is(roland)
learn abelard_vow when me.is(eldric)
--
[if me.is(roland)]
Under the ribs, a finger bone has been filed to a point against the stone, patiently, over what must have been weeks. It’s a very good pick. You take it, and say thank you, because someone should.

[if me.is(eldric)]
The surcoat was white once, with a rising sun. You know the signet: Abelard of the Dawn, who rode against the Hollow Host forty years ago carrying the order’s holy sword, and never came back. The songs say he swore the lich would never have his own blade. “He gave it to the deep.”

:: oubliette:scratches [act]
learn rhyme_flame
--
Tally marks, hundreds of them, and under them one line cut deep: FLAME FOR THE FOOL. HE HUMS IT WHEN HE’S PLEASED.

[if me.is(roland); append]
The rest is scraped away, or was never written. Whoever cut it stopped mid-word.

:: oubliette:look_up [act]
learn far_bolt
--
Through the bars: a room of bones, a long lever propped up by a wooden peg, and on the far door, an iron bolt shot home on this side.

[if me.is(roland); append]
A bolt is a small thing. It doesn’t need lifting. It needs sliding.

:: oubliette:tug_bolt [act]
set unbolted: yes
raise cleverness 1
retell: "From the bottom of the pit, Roland drew a bolt across the room with a crook of two fingers."
--
You crook two fingers and pull. Across the room above, the bolt grates, sticks, and slides free.

[if eldric.in(chapel); append]
From beyond that door, Eldric’s voice: “…Was that you?”

:: oubliette:climb [act]
move me to ossuary
raise trust 1 once
retell: "Roland climbed the knight’s chain out of the pit, and for once said nothing clever."
--
Hand over hand, up fifteen feet of chain that held Eldric to a pillar an hour ago. At the top a big hand closes on your wrist and hauls.

[once; append]
“Thank you,” you say, and find you mean it. Eldric looks as surprised as you are.

:: oubliette:hook [act]
set rope_down: yes
--
Third throw. The chain wraps a bar of the open grate and bites. Not dignified, but it holds.

:: oubliette:boost [act]
move roland to ossuary when attempt.success
--
Roland stands on your shoulders, then on your hands, then is gone over the lip. “I’ll fetch the chain,” he calls down. “Don’t go anywhere.”

[note]
If the chain is down here too, Eldric is alone in the pit with no way up. Should Roland fall back in as well, the rescue in the Host’s margin fires.

:: ossuary [room card:S]
item sluice: "the sluice lever" ~ like lever
item portcullis_lever: "a rusted lever by the portcullis" ~ like lever ~ with rusty: yes
inquest: "Rust can be broken, or it can be eased." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "There’s lamp oil in this prison. A rusted lever forced once is forced for good." ~ wits 3..
--
Bones line the walls in niches, sorted by size with terrible care. An iron grate is set in the floor. A long sluice lever is propped up by a wooden peg. By the north arch, a rusted lever stands beside a lowered portcullis.

[if bolted_door.open]
The east door stands unbolted.

[else]
The east door is bolted on this side.

[end]
> [[Lift the grate->ossuary:lift_grate]] ~ lift ~ when not grate.open
> [[Let your chain down into the pit->ossuary:lower_chain]] ~ cost 10 ~ when me.holds.chain and grate.open and not rope_down
> [[Draw the bolt on the east door->ossuary:bolt]] ~ cost 0 ~ when not bolted_door.open
> [[Knock out the sluice peg->ossuary:sluice]] ~ cost 10 ~ when not well.drained
> [[Force the rusted lever->ossuary:force_lever]] ~ force ~ when portcullis_lever.rusty
> [[Oil the rusted lever->ossuary:oil_lever]] ~ cost 10 ~ when me.holds.lamp_oil and portcullis_lever.rusty
> [[Pull the portcullis lever->ossuary:pull_lever]] ~ cost 10 ~ when portcullis_lever.oiled or portcullis_lever.mended

:: ossuary:lift_grate [act]
set grate_up: yes when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
You get your fingers under the bars and stand up. The grate comes with you, shrieking, and you lean it against the bones.

[else]
The grate lifts a finger’s width and drops. It wants a stronger back.

:: ossuary:lower_chain [act]
set rope_down: yes
--
You pay the chain out over the edge until it hangs within reach of the bottom, and brace your feet.

[if roland.in(oubliette); append]
“That’s my exit,” says a voice below. “I take back half of what I said in the cart.” “Only half?” “Let’s see how the climb goes.”

:: ossuary:bolt [act]
set unbolted: yes
--
You draw the bolt. It was never meant to be hard from this side.

:: ossuary:sluice [act]
set well.drained: yes
light flood when pov.any.in(oubliette) and not grate.open
retell: "The sluice opened, and the Well of the Eye drained away into the pit below."
--
The peg flies, the lever drops, and somewhere under the floor a great throat of water opens. Next door, the well begins to drain. The pipe in the pit begins to roar.

[if roland.in(oubliette) and not grate.open; append]
Below the grate, Roland, very calmly: “Eldric. Eldric. I have made a mistake.”

[note]
The flood fuse is the pit’s own trap: two turns to lift the grate, or the water lifts whoever’s down there into the bars. Lifting the grate in time floats them out.

:: ossuary:force_lever [act]
set portcullis_up: yes when attempt.success
set portcullis_lever.snapped: yes when attempt.success
set portcullis_lever.rusty: no when attempt.success
raise brute_force 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
You haul. The lever moves an inch, then all at once, and snaps off in your fist. The portcullis rattles up into the ceiling and stays there.

[else]
It doesn’t move. Rust holds it like a grudge.

:: ossuary:oil_lever [act]
set portcullis_lever.oiled: yes
set portcullis_lever.rusty: no
--
The rust drinks the oil with a faint hiss.

:: ossuary:pull_lever [act]
toggle portcullis_up
raise cleverness 1 once
--
[if portcullis.open]
The lever swings sweetly. The portcullis climbs into the dark.

[else]
The portcullis drops with a crash that shakes dust from the skulls.

:: chapel [room card:SE]
item altar: "an altar of the Dawn, overturned" ~ fixed
item glyph: "a ring of red sigils across the north threshold" ~ fixed
~ fact broken: no
~ fact frozen: no
inquest: "That ring of paint is the trap. Rings can be broken." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "The paint’s still wet. Scrape it, or freeze it." ~ wits 3..
--
[if eldric.chained and me.is(eldric)]
You wake against a pillar with your wrists in iron. The chain runs to a ring sunk in the stone, rusted, but as thick as your thumb.

[end]
A chapel of the Dawn, or it was. The altar lies on its face. Someone has painted a grinning mouth over the sunburst on the wall. The west door is shut fast. The north door stands open, but across its threshold runs a ring of red sigils.

[if glyph.broken]
The ring of sigils is cut through with a long scrape.

[if glyph.frozen]
Frost furs the sigils.

[end]
> [[Tear the ring out of the pillar->chapel:ring]]
~ force
~ cost rest
~ check might >= 5
~ for eldric
~ when eldric.chained
> [[Break down the west door->chapel:west_door]]
~ force
~ cost 40
~ check might >= 5
~ when not bolted_door.open and not eldric.chained
> [[Examine the sigils->chapel:sigils]] ~ examine
> [[Scrape through the ring with your chain->chapel:scrape]] ~ cost 20 ~ when me.holds.chain and not glyph.broken
> [[Frost the sigils->chapel:frost]] ~ chill ~ for roland ~ when not glyph.broken
> [[Right the altar->chapel:altar]] ~ lift ~ when not altar.righted and not eldric.chained
> [[Light the altar candle->chapel:candle]] ~ spark ~ for roland ~ when altar.righted and not altar.lit
> [[Keep vigil at the altar->chapel:vigil]] ~ vigil ~ for eldric ~ when altar.lit and not eldric.blessed

:: chapel:ring [act]
set eldric.chained: no
gain chain
raise brute_force 1
retell: "Eldric pulled the iron ring out of the pillar, stone and all."
--
You set your feet against the pillar and lean back until your shoulders crack. The stone gives first. The ring comes out with a fist of rock still on it, and now you have fifteen feet of chain and nobody holding the other end.

:: chapel:west_door [act]
set unbolted: yes when attempt.success
raise brute_force 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
Two kicks. The bolt tears out of the far side and the door slams open onto a room full of bones.

[else]
The door shudders in its frame and holds.

:: chapel:sigils [act]
learn glyph_lore
--
[if me.is(roland)]
The paint is still tacky. Whoever drew this did it recently, and badly. A glyph is only a ring with opinions: break the ring and it’s just paint.

[if me.is(eldric)]
Wardens of the Dawn are taught this before they’re taught to ride: a glyph is a ring. Cut the ring.

:: chapel:scrape [act]
set glyph.broken: yes
raise brute_force 1
--
You drag the chain’s end across the threshold. The ring of sigils splits with a sound like a struck match that doesn’t catch.

:: chapel:frost [act]
set glyph.frozen: yes until next chronon
raise cleverness 1
--
Frost spreads over the red paint until the sigils go dull and grey. It won’t last past the turn.

:: chapel:altar [act]
set altar.righted: yes when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
You set your shoulder to it and the altar rolls upright with a boom that rings through every room. On top, a candle stub, cold.

[else]
It doesn’t budge.

:: chapel:candle [act]
set altar.lit: yes
set altar.lit_by: me
--
A snap of your fingers. The candle catches and stands up very straight.

:: chapel:vigil [act]
set eldric.blessed: yes
raise trust 1 when altar.lit_by == roland
retell: "Eldric kept vigil at the defiled altar, and Roland, who believes in nothing he can’t pick, knelt beside him."
--
You kneel. For a long moment there is only the drip of water and the mouth painted on the wall. Then the candle stands up taller, as if someone had opened a window onto morning.

[if altar.lit_by == roland; append]
Roland, who believes in nothing he can’t pick, is kneeling too. He looks embarrassed about it. You don’t say anything. That seems like the kind thing.

:: chapel:glyph_fires [act]
--
The sigils light as you cross. Fire comes up out of the floor like a held breath let go.

[if me.is(roland); append]
It is very fast, and you are very small.

[if me.is(eldric); append]
You come through it with your hair smoking and a burn down one arm.

:: scriptorium [room card:W]
spot lectern: "the lectern"
item daybook: "the Host’s day-book, written backwards" ~ at lectern ~ fixed
item slab: "the lectern’s top, one slab of black stone the size of a coffin lid" ~ at lectern ~ fixed
learn carpet_sags when me.wits >= 3
inquest: "Stone that heavy hides something underneath." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "The writing runs backwards, like writing in a mirror. And he kept that slab where only a strong man could show it to you." ~ wits 3..
--
Shelves climb to the ceiling, and the air smells of paper slowly going to dust. A long red carpet runs from the door to a lectern of black stone at the far end. A lamp hangs on a hook by the door.

[if me.knows.carpet_sags]
The carpet sags in the middle, just slightly, like a hammock.

[if slab.raised]
Eldric is holding the lectern slab up on his shoulders, red in the face.

[end]
> [[Walk straight down the carpet->scriptorium:carpet]] ~ walk ~ when not me.at(lectern)
> [[Edge along the shelves to the lectern->scriptorium:shelves]]
~ cost 10
~ when me.knows.carpet_sags and not me.at(lectern)
> [[Tell Eldric to keep to the shelves->scriptorium:shelves]]
~ order eldric
~ when me.knows.carpet_sags and eldric.here
> [[Take the lamp->scriptorium:lamp]] ~ take lamp_oil
> [[Read the day-book->scriptorium:daybook]] ~ read ~ when me.at(lectern)
> [[Lift the lectern slab->scriptorium:slab]] ~ lift ~ cost 50 ~ check might >= 5 ~ when me.at(lectern)
> [[Lift the slab together->scriptorium:slab]] ~ together ~ when pov.all.at(lectern) and trust >= 1
> [[Read what’s carved underneath->scriptorium:underside]] ~ read ~ when slab.raised and me.at(lectern)
> [[Pick the lock on the north door->scriptorium:pick]] ~ pick ~ when not orrery_door.open
> [[Break down the north door->scriptorium:break]] ~ force ~ cost 40 ~ when not orrery_door.open

:: scriptorium:carpet [act]
move me to oubliette
set chute_found: yes
--
Halfway down, the carpet gives under you like a held breath. You drop through a hatch and down a long slick chute, and land, hard, at the bottom of the pit you started in.

[if me.knows.carpet_sags; append]
You saw it sag. You walked down it anyway. There’s a lesson here, and the Host is already laughing it at you.

:: scriptorium:shelves [act]
set me.at: lectern
--
Sideways, along the shelves, past a thousand spines. The carpet sags as you pass it, empty.

:: scriptorium:lamp [act]
--
A brass lamp, half full of oil. Light enough to carry, heavy enough to be useful.

:: scriptorium:daybook [act]
learn gave_up
learn rhyme_blink
raise cleverness 1 once
--
Every line runs right to left, every letter backwards. You read it the way you’d read a forger’s mirror-copy: slowly, and with a certain professional admiration.

“Year one of forever. The breath went first; I didn’t miss it. Then the warmth, which I did. And last, sleep. I have not slept since, so I built a game to pass the nights.”

In the margin, a doodle of a man stepping into a mirror, and four words: A BLINK FOR THE BOLD.

:: scriptorium:slab [act]
set slab.raised: yes until next act of eldric
raise brute_force 1
--
The slab comes up off its column with a grinding groan and settles on your shoulders. Something is carved on its underside.

[if not roland.at(lectern); append]
You squint at it upside down. Wizard’s scrawl. It means nothing to you, and you can’t hold this forever.

:: scriptorium:underside [act]
teach roland lodestone
raise trust 1 once
raise cleverness 1
retell: "Eldric held up a slab no two men should lift, while Roland read the spell carved under it."
--
Carved where only a strong man could show it to you: a spell of weight. Three words, and a thing becomes, for one breath, very, very heavy. You read it twice, then once more for luck.

“Done?” says Eldric, through his teeth. “Done.” The slab comes down like a door slammed by a god.

:: scriptorium:pick [act]
set orrery_unlocked: yes
raise cleverness 1
--
The lock is old and proud of itself. The finger bone teaches it humility.

:: scriptorium:break [act]
set orrery_unlocked: yes when attempt.success
raise brute_force 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
The door comes off its hinges, and its frame comes with it.

[else]
The door holds. Your shoulder doesn’t thank you.

:: well [room card:C]
item well_mirror: "the Great Eye" ~ like mirror
spot bottom: "the bottom of the well"
inquest: "Something down there wants fetching. Water can be dived, or let out." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "The pit you started in had a pipe. The sluice in the Ossuary decides where this water goes." ~ wits 3..
--
The middle room. A round shaft fills most of the floor, with black water a long way down. On the north wall hangs the largest mirror you have ever seen, framed in bone: an eye with no lid. Stairs climb north. A door leads west. To the east, a ledge drops into darkness.

[if well.drained]
The well is dry. Far down, in the mud, something long and straight catches the light.

[else]
Far down, under the black water, something catches the light, and is gone.

[if not well_mirror.open]
A bronze shutter covers the Eye.

[end]
> [[Look into the Great Eye->well:eye]] ~ examine ~ when well_mirror.open
> [[Anchor the chain and climb down->well:down]] ~ climb ~ when well.drained and me.holds.chain
> [[Dive for it->well:dive]]
~ cost rest
~ chance might in 6
~ for eldric
~ when not well.drained
> [[Take the longsword->well:sword]] ~ take abelard_sword ~ when me.at(bottom)
> [[Climb back up->well:up]] ~ climb ~ when me.at(bottom)
> [[Drop down the ledge->armory]] ~ walk ~ by ledge

:: well:eye [act]
lose vults 30
learn rhyme_sun
--
You look, and the Eye looks back, and you can’t look away. Somewhere in the glass, something is humming, very pleased with itself: “…and the sun for the grave.” When you can blink again, a long moment has gone.

[if me.is(roland); append]
A long moment, for a line of verse. You’d call it a fair trade if he hadn’t enjoyed it so much.

:: well:down [act]
set me.at: bottom
--
You loop the chain round the well-head and go down hand over hand into the cold.

:: well:dive [act]
gain abelard_sword when attempt.success
wound 1 when not attempt.success
raise brute_force 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
The cold hits like a wall. You go down blind, find the mud, find a hilt, and come up with a sword and no feeling in your hands.

[else]
The cold closes your throat. You come up empty, coughing, with your heart pounding wrong.

:: well:sword [act]
--
A good plain longsword, under forty years of silt.

[if me.knows.abelard_vow; append]
Abelard’s. He gave it to the deep, the songs said, and here it is: not lost, only hidden where a lich would never look. Down.

:: well:up [act]
set me.at: nothing
--
Up the chain, out of the cold.

:: armory [room card:E]
item statue_lever: "the statue lever" ~ like lever ~ with rusty: yes
item planet_lever: "the planet lever" ~ like lever
item eye_lever: "the eye lever" ~ like lever
inquest: "Three carvings, three mirrors." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "Close the right mirror and something in the Gallery stops being watched." ~ wits 3..
--
Racks of weapons, rusted to lace. Along the north wall stand three levers, each under a small carving: a statue, a planet, an open eye. The statue lever is red with rust. A spiral stair climbs into the dark. High on the west wall, a ledge overhangs, too high to reach. South, a door to the chapel.

[end]
> [[Search the racks->armory:racks]] ~ examine
> [[Pull the planet lever->armory:planet]] ~ cost 10
> [[Pull the eye lever->armory:eye]] ~ cost 10
> [[Force the statue lever->armory:force_statue]] ~ force ~ when statue_lever.rusty
> [[Oil the statue lever->armory:oil_statue]] ~ cost 10 ~ when me.holds.lamp_oil and statue_lever.rusty
> [[Pull the statue lever->armory:pull_statue]] ~ cost 10 ~ when statue_lever.oiled or statue_lever.mended
> [[Mend the snapped lever->armory:mend]] ~ mend ~ for roland ~ when statue_lever.snapped

:: armory:racks [act]
set armory.searched: yes when me.is(eldric)
gain rustblade when me.is(eldric)
--
[if me.is(eldric)]
Most of it is rust holding hands. But a soldier knows where to look: at the back of the third rack, a notched arming sword with sound steel under the scale. You take it, and your hand stops feeling empty.

[if me.is(roland)]
Rust. Rust. A halberd that is mostly a rumour. Nothing you’d trust with your life, and you’d know.

:: armory:planet [act]
toggle orrery_mirror.open
--
Two rooms away, something slams. Or opens. You’d have to go and look.

:: armory:eye [act]
toggle well_mirror.open
--
Next door, bronze rings on bronze.

:: armory:force_statue [act]
set gallery_mirror.open: no when attempt.success
set statue_lever.snapped: yes when attempt.success
set statue_lever.rusty: no when attempt.success
raise brute_force 1 when attempt.success
--
[if attempt.success]
The lever comes down and keeps coming, and snaps. Far off, a shutter crashes shut. It’s staying shut.

[else]
The lever doesn’t move.

:: armory:oil_statue [act]
set statue_lever.oiled: yes
set statue_lever.rusty: no
--
The rust drinks the oil and goes dark.

:: armory:pull_statue [act]
toggle gallery_mirror.open
raise cleverness 1 once
--
The lever swings. Up in the Gallery, a shutter slides.

:: armory:mend [act]
set statue_lever.mended: yes
set statue_lever.snapped: no
raise cleverness 1
--
Mend is for torn pages and split lips. Nobody told the lever that. The broken pin knits, a little crooked, and the lever swings again.

:: orrery [room card:NW]
item orrery_mirror: "a round mirror aimed at the sun" ~ like mirror
fact ember: 2 ~ of 6
fact tide: 0 ~ of 6
fact crown: 4 ~ of 6
let hours: ["dawn", "morning", "noon", "dusk", "evening", "midnight"]
let aligned: orrery.ember == orrery.tide and orrery.tide == orrery.crown
learn heart_is_life when me.wits >= 3 and orrery_mirror.open
inquest: "The three planets move at different speeds." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "Count how far each planet moves for one turn of the crank." ~ wits 3..
--
A brass orrery fills the room. At its heart hangs a sun the size of a man’s head, gleaming as if lit from inside. A bright rod pierces it top to bottom, and above the sun the rod ends in a short crossbar, like a crown. Three planets ride their rings: red Ember at {hours[orrery.ember]}, blue Tide at {hours[orrery.tide]}, gold Crown at {hours[orrery.crown]}. A crank stands at the rim. A plaque is set in the base.

[if orrery_mirror.open]
A round mirror on the wall is aimed at the sun, and nowhere else.

[else]
A bronze shutter covers a round mirror on the wall.

[if here.has(jester)]
In the corner stands a stone Jester with a painted grin, one foot raised as if mid-dance.

[if aligned and not lumen.taken]
The three planets kneel in one line. The rod through the sun stands a little proud of it.

[if lumen.taken and here.has(heart)]
The sun sits loose in its cradle, and it is beating.

[if lumen.lost]
The orrery is a wreck of bent rings. The rod is jammed through the middle of it, beyond anyone’s drawing.

[end]
> [[Read the plaque->orrery:plaque]] ~ examine
> [[Turn the crank->orrery:crank]] ~ crank ~ when not lumen.taken and not lumen.lost
> [[Examine the sun->orrery:sun]] ~ examine
> [[Spark the rod->orrery:spark]] ~ spark ~ for roland
> [[Draw the rod->orrery:draw]] ~ cost 20 ~ when aligned and not lumen.taken
> [[Lift out the sun->orrery:take_heart]] ~ take heart ~ when lumen.taken
> [[Wrench the sun off its axle->orrery:wrench]]
~ force
~ cost rest
~ check might >= 5
~ for eldric
~ when not lumen.taken and not lumen.lost
> [[Watch the Jester->orrery]] ~ observe ~ when here.has(jester)

:: orrery:plaque [act]
--
WHEN THE WANDERERS KNEEL IN ONE LINE, THE AXIS MAY BE DRAWN.

:: orrery:crank [act]
raise orrery.ember 1 mod 6
raise orrery.tide 2 mod 6
raise orrery.crown 3 mod 6
--
Gears tick under the floor. Ember creeps to {hours[orrery.ember]}. Tide swings to {hours[orrery.tide]}. Crown sweeps round to {hours[orrery.crown]}.

[if aligned; append]
All three stop in a line, and something deep in the sun goes click.

:: orrery:sun [act]
learn lumen_lore when me.is(eldric)
--
[if me.is(eldric)]
That crossbar above the sun isn’t a crown. It’s a quillon. That is a hilt, and you know it: the white hilt of Lumen, the holy sword of your order, which drinks any spell that strikes it. They built the orrery around a sword.

[if me.is(roland)]
It’s warm. Nothing heats it. Hold your hand close and it beats, slow as a sleeper’s heart.

[if me.knows.heart_is_life; append]
A lich keeps his life somewhere outside his body. This one keeps a mirror on it day and night. You would too.

:: orrery:spark [act]
learn drinks_magic
--
You flick a spark at the rod. It gutters as it gets close, and goes out, as if something drank it.

:: orrery:draw [act]
gain lumen when me.is(eldric)
raise cleverness 1
retell: "Eldric drew Lumen out of the orrery like a sword from a stone, because it was one."
--
[if me.is(eldric)]
It slides out of the sun like a sword from a scabbard, because it is one. Lumen is lighter than it looks and colder than it should be, and the edge has never been nicked. It knows your hand.

[if me.is(roland)]
You take hold of the hilt, and it bites cold into your palm. It won’t come for you. Whatever this is, it wants a hand that prays.

:: orrery:take_heart [act]
set hask.saw_heart: yes when orrery_mirror.open
retell: "They took the Hollow Host’s heart out of his orrery."
--
You lift the sun out of its cradle. It beats against your palms, slow, offended.

[if orrery_mirror.open; append]
Every mirror in the prison turns to look at you.

[else]
Behind its shutter, the round mirror sees nothing at all.

:: orrery:wrench [act]
set heart.cracked: yes
set lumen.lost: yes
set hask.saw_heart: yes
gain heart
light collapse
raise brute_force 1
retell: "Eldric tore the sun off its axle, and the Ninefold Cell began to fall."
--
You get both arms round the sun and heave. The rings bend, the rod bends, and the sun comes away with a sound like a bell thrown down a stair. Something inside it cracks. Every mirror in the prison screams, and dust begins to sift from the ceiling.

:: gallery [room card:N]
item gallery_mirror: "a tall black mirror facing the statues" ~ like mirror
inquest: "The statues have moved before. Look at the floor." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "They only dance when nothing’s looking. Something is always looking in here." ~ wits 3..
--
A long hall of plinths. On two stand statues: a Knight in stone plate, twice the size of a man, and a Widow in a stone veil with her hands half raised. The third plinth is empty. Arches open west and east, and stairs lead down.

[if gallery_mirror.open]
A tall black mirror faces the statues from the south wall.

[else]
A bronze shutter covers the tall mirror on the south wall.

[if not here.has(knight)]
The Knight’s plinth stands empty.

[end]
> [[Examine the floor->gallery:floor]] ~ examine
> [[Look into the tall mirror->gallery:mirror]] ~ examine ~ when gallery_mirror.open
> [[Push the Knight east->gallery:push]] ~ push ~ for eldric ~ when here.has(knight)
> [[Tell Eldric to push it with his eyes shut->gallery:push_blind]]
~ order eldric
~ push
~ when me.knows.statue_rule and eldric.here and here.has(knight)
> [[Watch the statues->gallery]] ~ observe ~ when here.has(knight) or here.has(widow)

:: gallery:floor [act]
learn statue_rule when me.is(roland)
--
Scuffs in the dust: long curved scrapes, plinth to arch and back again.

[if me.is(roland); append]
They’ve moved, and not by being dragged: the scrapes are footsteps. Yet they never move while you’re here, and that mirror never looks away from them. Statues that move only when nothing is watching. You’ve read about worse.

[if me.is(eldric); append]
Someone’s been dragging furniture.

:: gallery:mirror [act]
--
Your reflection, the statues behind it, and for half a heartbeat a tall paper man standing among them, smiling. Then just the statues.

:: gallery:push [act]
--
[if gallery_mirror.open or not me.blind]
You set your shoulder to the Knight and shove. It won’t move. It’s as if the stone is holding its breath while you look at it.

[note]
A plain push always fails: the pusher is looking. Only an order from someone who knows the rule makes it work.

:: gallery:push_blind [act]
set me.blind: yes
move knight to gate when not gallery_mirror.open
move me to gate when not gallery_mirror.open
raise trust 1 once when not gallery_mirror.open
raise brute_force 1 when not gallery_mirror.open
retell: "On Roland’s word, and against all sense, Eldric shut his eyes and pushed a stone knight through a wall of air."
--
[if gallery_mirror.open]
“Shut my eyes,” Eldric says. He does. Nothing moves. “Something’s still watching it,” you realise aloud. The mirror.

[else]
“Shut my eyes,” Eldric says flatly. “And push.” He does. The Knight slides like a boat leaving the shore, through the arch, and onto the great pan before the Gate, which sinks under it with a groan of chains. Eldric opens his eyes, looks at what he did, and looks at you. You shrug: he did the pushing.

:: gate [room card:NE]
fact sun_seal: no
fact mouth_seal: no
fact scale_seal: no
inquest: "Each lock says what it wants." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "His heart, his guardian, and what he gave up, in order." ~ wits 3..
--
The door is black iron, twice Eldric’s height, with no handle. Three locks are set in it: a socket shaped like a sun, a stone mouth with parted lips, and, on the floor before it, a great iron pan hung on chains like one side of a scale. Words are cut above each.

[if gate.scale_seal]
The stone Knight stands on the pan, which has sunk to the floor.

[if here.has(widow)]
The Widow stands by the door, hands half raised, much closer than you left her.

[if gate.sun_seal]
The sun sits in its socket, beating.

[if gate.mouth_seal]
The stone mouth is closed and smiling.

[end]
> [[Read the words over the locks->gate:words]] ~ examine
> [[Stand on the pan->gate:pan]] ~ cost 0 ~ when not gate.scale_seal
> [[Set the sun in its socket->gate:sun]] ~ cost 10 ~ when me.holds.heart and not gate.sun_seal
> [[Speak three cantrips into the mouth->gate:mouth]] ~ cost 30 ~ for roland ~ when not gate.mouth_seal
> [[Open the door->threshold]] ~ walk ~ when gate.sun_seal and gate.mouth_seal and gate.scale_seal
> [[Watch the Widow->gate]] ~ observe ~ when here.has(widow)

:: gate:words [act]
--
Over the sun: ONLY MY HEART OPENS MY DOOR.

Over the mouth: GIVE BACK WHAT I GAVE FOR FOREVER, IN THE ORDER I GAVE IT.

Over the pan: LET A GUARDIAN OF STONE STAND HERE IN MY PLACE.

:: gate:pan [act]
--
[if pov.all.here]
You both stand on it. The pan sinks two fingers’ width, and stops.

[else]
The pan sinks a finger’s width under you, and stops. It wants far more than a man.

:: gate:sun [act]
set gate.sun_seal: yes
set gate.sun_setter: me
--
The sun fits its socket exactly. Something behind the iron unlatches, and the heart goes on beating in the door.

[note]
The heart comes back out when the door opens. Whoever set it there is holding it again on the threshold.

:: gate:mouth [act]
{choose input for: mouth_words, from: cantrip, length: 3}
set gate.mouth_seal: yes when mouth_words == [gust, spark, hush]
raise cleverness 1 when gate.mouth_seal
lose vults rest when not gate.mouth_seal
--
[if mouth_words == [gust, spark, hush]]
The mouth takes your breath, then your warmth, then the small silence after, and its lips close with a click like a satisfied sigh.

[else]
The mouth laughs at you, and frost comes out of it.

:: party_bar [lib everywhere]
> [[Switch to Eldric->here]] ~ switch ~ for roland
> [[Switch to Roland->here]] ~ switch ~ for eldric
> [[Spend an Inquest->here]] ~ inquest ~ when inquests > 0
> [[Tie the Backward Knot->rewind]] ~ backward_knot ~ for roland ~ when roland.rewinds > 0 and eldric.alive
> [[Pray for the hour back->rewind]] ~ second_dawn ~ for eldric ~ when eldric.rewinds > 0
> [[End the turn->here]] ~ pass

:: again [interlude]
The world folds up like a cheap theatre, and the Hollow Host claps.

[if here.in(prison)]
You wake where you began: Roland in the pit, Eldric in chains, every lock relocked. Only what you learned came with you.

[else]
You wake on the threshold, with everything you carried out of the cells.

:: threshold [checkpoint]
checkpoint threshold
give heart to gate.sun_setter
--
The door swings in on silence. Beyond it, a stair climbs toward candlelight.

[if collapse.lit]
Behind you, with a long tired roar, the Ninefold Cell finishes falling in.

[if cleverness > brute_force]
“Well!” says the Host, from up the stair. “You think. I do like that in a guest. Come up.”

[else]
“Well,” says the Host, from up the stair. “You certainly hit things. Come up.”

[end]
> [[Climb to the sanctum->sanctum]] ~ walk

:: hask_duel [npc]
--
stat wards: 3
stat wards: 2 when heart.cracked

pattern rhyme: flame, frost, blink, sunfall ~ repeat ~ one per round
~ recall first when hask.saw_heart and holder != nobody and not heart.cracked
~ falter instead of sunfall when holder != nobody and not heart.cracked

spell flame: at roland ~ then wound target 1
~ blocked by shield, absorb, parry, interrupt ~ redirected by guard
spell frost: at eldric ~ then freeze target
~ kill target when target.frozen
~ blocked by shield, absorb, interrupt
spell blink: through mirror ~ then set hask.dodging: yes
~ then set hask.grounded: yes next round
~ fails when count(mirror, in: here, open: yes) == 0 or hask.pinned
~ on fail: set hask.grounded: yes
spell sunfall: at pov.all ~ then kill target
~ blocked by shield, absorb
spell recall: at holder ~ then take heart
~ blocked by shield, absorb, guard
spell falter: ~ then nothing

:: sanctum [encounter]
encounter hask
~ round by round
~ countdown 3s per act
~ plus 2s when inquest
~ timeout stay
~ hask casts last
~ until hask.wards == 0 or pov.all.down
item east_mirror: "the east mirror" ~ like mirror
item west_mirror: "the west mirror" ~ like mirror
--
A round room, all candles. Two tall mirrors face each other across it. A yard above the floor hangs the Hollow Host: a tall man made of very old paper, in a magister’s robe, with two coals for eyes and a smile he has clearly practised.

“Three wards,” he says, and touches the air around him. It rings like glass.

[if heart.cracked; append]
He looks at the cracked sun in your hands, and his smile thins. “Two, then. Vandals.”

[if pov.any.knows.rhyme_flame and pov.any.knows.rhyme_frost and pov.any.knows.rhyme_blink and pov.any.knows.rhyme_sun]
You know his rhyme, every line. You know what he does first.

[end]
> [[Begin->sanctum:round]] ~ cost 0

:: sanctum:round [round]
let next: hask.rhyme.next
inquest: "Watch his hands. They tell you what’s coming." ~ wits ..=2
inquest: "He’ll do what the rhyme says next. Answer it before he finishes." ~ wits 3..
--
[if next == flame]
He draws a line of red across the air with one finger.

[if next == flame and pov.any.knows.rhyme_flame; append]
Flame for the fool. He’s looking at Roland.

[if next == frost]
The floor rimes over, creeping toward Eldric.

[if next == frost and pov.any.knows.rhyme_frost; append]
Frost for the brave.

[if next == blink]
His eyes go to the mirrors: one, then the other.

[if next == blink and pov.any.knows.rhyme_blink; append]
A blink for the bold. Next round he’ll come out on foot.

[if next == sunfall]
He cups his hands, and the candlelight drains into them.

[if next == sunfall and pov.any.knows.rhyme_sun; append]
The sun for the grave. Anyone unshielded dies.

[if next == recall]
He holds out a hand toward his heart, palm up, like a man asking for his hat back.

[if next == falter]
He cups his hands, looks at his heart in your keeping, and lets the light go.

[if hask.grounded]
He is on the floor, on his own two feet, within reach of a sword.

[if eldric.frozen]
Eldric is cased in ice to the shoulders.

[end]
> [[Ember Lance at Eldric’s ice->sanctum:lance]] ~ ember_lance ~ for roland ~ when eldric.frozen
> [[Rime Shield on yourself->sanctum:shield]] ~ rime_shield ~ for roland ~ with {target: roland}
> [[Rime Shield on Eldric->sanctum:shield]] ~ rime_shield ~ for roland ~ with {target: eldric}
> [[Frostglass the east mirror->sanctum:frostglass]] ~ frostglass ~ for roland ~ with {mirror: east_mirror}
> [[Frostglass the west mirror->sanctum:frostglass]] ~ frostglass ~ for roland ~ with {mirror: west_mirror}
> [[Thunderclap->sanctum:thunderclap]] ~ thunderclap ~ for roland
> [[Lodestone->sanctum:lodestone]] ~ lodestone ~ for roland ~ when roland.knows.lodestone
> [[Hold up his heart->sanctum:show_heart]] ~ cost 10 ~ when me.holds.heart and not hask.shown_heart

> [[Strike->sanctum:strike]] ~ strike ~ for eldric ~ when hask.grounded and me.holds.any(sword) and not eldric.frozen
> [[Guard Roland->sanctum:guard]] ~ guard ~ for eldric ~ when not eldric.frozen
> [[Raise Lumen->sanctum:absorb]] ~ guard ~ for eldric ~ when me.holds.lumen and not eldric.frozen
> [[Shatter a mirror->sanctum:shatter]] ~ force ~ cost 20 ~ for eldric ~ when not eldric.frozen
> [[Smash his heart->sanctum:smash]] ~ force ~ cost 20 ~ for eldric ~ when me.holds.heart and not eldric.frozen
> [[Hand him the heart->sanctum:hand_over]] ~ cost 0 ~ for roland ~ when me.holds.heart

> [[As one->sanctum:as_one]]
~ cost 30 from roland
~ cost 20 from eldric
~ when trust == 3 and eldric.holds.lumen and not eldric.frozen
~ for pov
> [[Let him cast->sanctum:spell]] ~ pass ~ ends turn

:: sanctum:lance [act]
set eldric.frozen: no
--
Spark, gust, spark: a lance of fire, aimed with great care at your only friend. The ice goes to steam. “Warn me next time.” “I just did.”

:: sanctum:shield [act]
shield target
--
Chill, mend, chill. Ice grows over {target.name} in a clear shell, sealing its own cracks as fast as they come.

:: sanctum:frostglass [act]
set mirror.open: no
--
Chill and gust: frost runs across {mirror.name} until it shows nothing at all.

:: sanctum:thunderclap [act]
interrupt hask when next in [flame, frost]
--
Hush, gust, spark: you gather a silence, throw it, and let it go all at once. The crack slaps every candle flat.

[if next in [flame, frost]; append]
The Host flinches, and whatever he was weaving comes apart in his fingers.

[else]
He winces, but whatever he’s building is too big to drop.

:: sanctum:lodestone [act]
set hask.grounded: yes
pin hask
--
Three words of weight. The Host drops out of the air like a dropped cloak and hits the flagstones on his knees, very surprised, and very, very heavy.

:: sanctum:show_heart [act]
set hask.shown_heart: yes
skip hask this round when not hask.saw_heart
--
You hold up the brass sun. It beats in your hand.

[if not hask.saw_heart]
The Host stops in the air. For the first time since the cart, he has nothing to say. “That’s— where did— that is mine.” For a whole breath he forgets to cast anything at all.

[else]
“Yes, yes, I saw you take it,” he says. “Do be careful with it.”

:: sanctum:strike [act]
lower hask.wards 2 when me.holds.lumen and lumen.charged
lower hask.wards 1 when not (me.holds.lumen and lumen.charged)
set lumen.charged: no
--
[if hask.dodging]
He isn’t there. The edge passes through a smear of old paper and candlelight.

[else]
[if me.holds.lumen and lumen.charged]
Lumen lets go of everything it has drunk, all at once, down the length of one stroke. Two of his wards break together, like two windows in a storm.

[if not (me.holds.lumen and lumen.charged)]
Steel meets a ward, and the ward rings, and cracks, and falls away like a pane of glass.

:: sanctum:guard [act]
guard roland
~ parry with abelard_sword
~ absorb with lumen
--
You step in front of Roland. Whatever comes for him will have to come through you.

:: sanctum:absorb [act]
absorb with lumen
set lumen.charged: yes when absorbed
--
You raise Lumen like a lamp in a dark room.

:: sanctum:shatter [act]
set mirror.open: no
--
You put a fist, or a sword, through the nearest mirror. Glass rains. The Host makes a small hurt noise, as if you’d trodden on his foot.

:: sanctum:smash [act]
set hask.mortal: yes
set heart.cracked: yes
lower hask.wards 1
destroy heart
raise brute_force 1
retell: "Eldric set the Host’s heart on the flagstones and broke it under his heel."
--
You set the sun on the flagstones and bring your heel down. It breaks like a bell. The Host screams with every mirror in the room, and for the first time he looks like what he is: old paper, and nothing holding it together.

:: sanctum:hand_over [act]
give heart to eldric
--
You toss Eldric the sun. He catches it one-handed, as if he’d been catching hearts all his life.

:: sanctum:as_one [act]
lower hask.wards 2
retell: "Roland poured an Ember Lance into Lumen, and Eldric cut the air in half."
--
Roland doesn’t aim at the lich. He aims at Eldric’s sword: spark, gust, spark, poured into the blade. Lumen drinks the lance and turns white, and Eldric cuts the air in half. The light goes where the edge points. The Host, floating, untouchable, is suddenly neither.

:: sanctum:spell [resolve]
--
[if cast.spell == flame and cast.outcome == hit]
Fire takes Roland full in the chest.

[if cast.spell == flame and cast.outcome == guarded]
Eldric takes the fire meant for Roland on his own chest, and staggers, and stays up.

[if cast.spell == flame and cast.outcome == parried]
Eldric turns the flame aside on Abelard’s blade, and it splashes harmless across the floor.

[if cast.spell == frost and cast.outcome == hit]
Ice climbs Eldric to the shoulders and holds him fast.

[if cast.spell == blink and cast.outcome == hit]
He steps into a mirror and out of the other, and lands on his feet, laughing.

[if cast.spell == blink and cast.outcome == failed]
He throws himself at the glass and hits frost, hard. He lands on the flagstones in a heap of robes.

[if cast.spell == sunfall and cast.outcome == hit]
Light, all of it, everywhere at once.

[if cast.spell == recall and cast.outcome == hit]
The heart leaps from your hand to his, like a dog called home.

[if cast.outcome == shielded]
The spell breaks on Roland’s ice and runs off it like rain off a window.

[if cast.outcome == absorbed]
Lumen drinks the spell whole and begins to glow.

[if cast.outcome == interrupted]
Nothing comes. The spell died in his hands.

[if cast.spell == falter]
Nothing. He will not burn his own heart, and he knows you know it.

[end]
> [[Next round->sanctum:round]] ~ when hask.wards > 0 and pov.any.up
> [[He falls->fallen]] ~ when hask.wards == 0

:: fallen [finale]
--
The last ward breaks. The Hollow Host comes down out of the air like a kite with its string cut, and lies on the flagstones, and is suddenly very small.

[if hask.mortal]
Without his heart, there is nothing to put him back. He looks at the two of you with mild interest, says “Oh. Nicely done,” and comes apart into ash and old pages.

[else]
“You’ll want to do something about my heart,” he says, from the floor, with a little of his old cheer. “Or I’ll be back. I’m very patient.”

[end]
> [[Smash the heart->ending_dawn]] ~ for eldric ~ when not hask.mortal and pov.any.holds.heart
> [[Keep the heart->ending_scholar]] ~ for roland ~ when not hask.mortal and pov.any.holds.heart
> [[Carry it home to the Dawn together->ending_vigil]] ~ for pov ~ when not hask.mortal and trust == 3
> [[Climb out into the morning->ending_dawn]] ~ when hask.mortal

:: ending_dawn [ending]
--
They climbed out of the Host’s house at sunrise, a thief and a knight, both of them filthy, neither of them dead.

[if eldric.holds.lumen]
Eldric carried Lumen home to an order that had stopped hoping for it.

[end]
Roland, at the crossroads, offered his hand. Eldric looked at it for a long moment, the way you’d look at a lock, and took it.

:: ending_scholar [ending]
--
Roland kept the heart. He told Eldric it was for study, and Eldric let him say it.

It sits in a box on Roland’s desk to this day, beating slowly, waiting. Some nights, when Roland reads late, he could swear it hums.

:: ending_vigil [ending]
--
They carried the heart between them, a week on foot, to the first chapel of the Dawn they found, and laid it under the altar, and kept vigil over it a night and a day: the knight praying, the thief keeping the candle lit.

In the morning there was only brass, cold, and the beat had stopped.

:: retelling [retell]
retell: past tense ~ third person ~ by turn
~ skip examine when nothing learned
~ merge walk
~ one chapter per room, on first visit
~ fold deaths into “Again, and again.”
--
{retold}

[if cleverness > brute_force]
And the Host, who kept score, wrote in his day-book in a very small hand: CLEVER.

[else]
And the Host, who kept score, wrote in his day-book in a very small hand: STRONG. THEN CLEVER. EVENTUALLY.
